-- WAY W1-NOW: the chosen way (W1), but the reader gate compares NOW with the Gazette's own instant,
-- 31 October 2012 at 5.00 pm Singapore time, instead of comparing TODAY with the date 31 October 2012.
--
-- A system-time pin is a DATE (finding 4), and a date pin is 00:00 UTC, which is 08:00 in Singapore.
-- So a reader pinned to 31 October 2012 reads at 08:00, before 5.00 pm, and is told the old law for the whole day.
-- Printed output is in alt-w1-now-gate.out; walkthrough step 7.
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT datetime
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

DECLARE `Version of the First Schedule` IS ONE OF
    `the First Schedule of three items`
    `the First Schedule of the TVRO system only`

`the Gazette instant` MEANS Datetime (Date 31 10 2012) 17 0 0

`the text, with the reader gate on NOW` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` BELOW (Date 31 7 2003)
           THEN REFUSE "not covered: the conduct day is before the first deposited edition (31 July 2003)"
           IF     `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011)
              AND NOW AT LEAST `the Gazette instant`
           THEN `the First Schedule of the TVRO system only`
           OTHERWISE `the First Schedule of three items`

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Version of the First Schedule`
`the text under this way` MEANS
    `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` reading (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` conduct `the text, with the reader gate on NOW`)

-- BEGIN GENERATED PAIRS (build-walkthrough.py: the same conduct-day and reading-day pairs in every file)
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012)   -- P01
